  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The race for Missouri's 4th Congressional District takes place under a new congressional map signed into law in September 2025 by Governor Mike Kehoe, which redrew district boundaries to include part of Kansas City and shifted the district's political composition. Incumbent Republican Rep. Mark Alford, a former television news anchor first elected in 2022, is seeking a third term and faces primary challengers from Heather Shelton and Scott Vincent Vera. Seven Democratic candidates are competing in their party's primary on August 4, 2026, with the winner advancing to face the Republican nominee and Libertarian Thomas Holbrook in the November general election. The redistricting plan has been controversial and faced legal challenges and a citizen-led referendum effort, adding uncertainty to the electoral landscape.",
